{"name":"Lightning Bug","hex":"#efde74","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lightning bug","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of firefly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lightning_bug"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firefly","blocks":[{"text":"The Lampyridae are a family of elateroid beetles with more than 2,400 described species, many of which are light-emitting. They are soft-bodied beetles commonly called fireflies, lightning bugs, or glowworms for their conspicuous emission of light, mainly during twilight, to attract mates. The type species is Lampyris noctiluca, the common glow-worm of Europe. Light production in the Lampyridae is thought to have originated as a warning signal that the larvae were distasteful. This ability to create light was then co-opted as a mating signal and, in a further development, adult female fireflies of the genus Photuris mimic the flash pattern of the Photinus beetle to trap their males as prey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg/330px-Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefly","wikidata":"Q25420"},{"title":"Photinus (beetle)","blocks":[{"text":"The rover fireflies (Photinus) are a genus of fireflies. They are the type genus of tribe Photinini in subfamily Lampyrinae. This genus contains, for example, the common eastern firefly, the most common species of firefly in North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Eastern_Firefly_%2814614518144%29.jpg/330px-Eastern_Firefly_%2814614518144%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photinus_(beetle)","wikidata":"Q3039833"},{"title":"Lightning Bug (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lightning Bug is a 2004 coming-of-age drama film. It is the debut film by writer/director and SFX makeup artist Robert Green Hall. The film is a fictionalized account of Hall's own childhood and entry into special effects makeup for film and television. It was filmed on location Fairview, Alabama. It was executive produced by Laura Prepon."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/LightningBug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning_Bug_(film)","wikidata":"Q6546427"},{"title":"Lightning","blocks":[{"text":"Lightning is a natural phenomenon consisting of electrostatic discharges occurring through the atmosphere between two electrically charged regions. One or both regions are within the atmosphere, with the second region sometimes occurring on the ground. Following the lightning, the regions become partially or wholly electrically neutralized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning","wikidata":"Q33741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALampyris_Noctiluca_(firefly)_mating.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A larviform female with light-emitting organs on her abdomen. Unlike larvae, she has compound eyes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuciola4_crop.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photuris female by flash photography (above); by her own light (below)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirefly_composite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/500px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/960px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/500px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg/500px-GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg/960px-GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Gl